From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 03:06:06 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Offer raw as ten bit mode over the eight bit bus

The ITU8 packing gives two bytes per pixel -- ten bits of data in a
sixteen bit container, high byte first, values spanning 0 to 1023 -- so a
2592 pixel line occupies 5184 bytes and nothing downstream can take it.

All sixteen values of the byte order register were swept through the
module parameter and every one of them does that. The register only
chooses which byte comes first: eight of the values put the data byte
second and eight put it first, and none produces one byte per pixel.
There is no eight bit raw mode on this sensor.

So use the ten bit mode, one pixel per clock, and keep the media bus code
at eight bits because that is what the receiver sees. The A711 camera
module brings out eight data lines, D0 to D7, and a ten bit sensor on an
eight bit bus is wired most significant bits first, so the CSI gets bits
9:2 and the bottom two are lost. That is a plain eight bit bayer frame,
which is what both the CSI and the ISP behind it already take.

The alignment is the assumption here. If the module wired the low eight
instead, the capture will be noise rather than an image, and say so.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 38 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -515,30 +515,40 @@ static const struct hm5065_pixfmt hm5065_formats[] = {
 	/*
 	 * Raw bayer, the sensor's own processing bypassed. The colour
 	 * pipeline is what the ISP behind this is being characterised
-	 * against, so being able to hand it an unprocessed frame -- and one
-	 * carrying a test pattern that is injected before that pipeline, so
-	 * it arrives as a known mosaic -- is the point of this entry.
+	 * against, so handing it an unprocessed frame -- carrying a test
+	 * pattern injected before that pipeline, so it arrives as a known
+	 * mosaic -- is the point of this entry.
+	 *
+	 * The sensor is put in its ten bit mode, one pixel per clock, but
+	 * the code is eight bit because that is what the receiver sees: the
+	 * A711 camera module brings out eight data lines, D0 to D7, and a
+	 * ten bit sensor on an eight bit bus is wired most significant bits
+	 * first. So the CSI gets bits 9:2 and the bottom two are lost, which
+	 * is a plain eight bit bayer frame.
+	 *
+	 * Not the ITU8 packing, which was tried first: it gives two bytes
+	 * per pixel, ten bits of data in a sixteen bit container, so a 2592
+	 * pixel line occupies 5184 bytes and nothing downstream can take it.
+	 * All sixteen values of the byte order register were swept and every
+	 * one of them does that -- the register only chooses which byte
+	 * comes first. There is no eight bit raw mode on this sensor.
 	 *
 	 * The phase is a guess until it is measured off the CSI the way the
-	 * gc2145 one was. So is the bus setup value: 0x7000 selects byte and
-	 * component order and the vendor never used it for raw, its own raw
-	 * format table being present but empty.
+	 * gc2145 one was, and so is the bus setup value: the vendor never
+	 * used raw here, its own raw format table being present and empty.
 	 */
 	{
 		.code              = MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SBGGR8_1X8,
 		.colorspace        = V4L2_COLORSPACE_RAW,
-		.data_fmt          = HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU8,
+		.data_fmt          = HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU10,
 		.ycbcr_order       = HM5065_REG_YCRCB_ORDER_Y_CB_Y_CR,
 		.fmt_setup         = 0x08
 	},
 };
 
 /*
- * Raw arrives as two bytes per pixel, ten bits of data in a sixteen bit
- * container, and the ISP downstream can only take eight. Register 0x7000
- * selects byte and component order over sixteen values and the vendor
- * never used it for raw, so which of them gives one byte per pixel -- if
- * any does -- has to be found by trying them.
+ * Register 0x7000 selects byte and component order and the vendor never
+ * used it for raw, so the right value has to be found by trying them.
  *
  * It cannot be swept from userspace: writing 0x7000 while the sensor is
  * streaming stalls it, and outside streaming the chip is powered down and
@@ -552,8 +562,8 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(raw_bus_format,
 
 static bool hm5065_format_is_raw(const struct hm5065_pixfmt *fmt)
 {
-	return fmt->data_fmt == HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU8 ||
-	       fmt->data_fmt == HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU10;
+	return fmt->data_fmt == HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU10 ||
+	       fmt->data_fmt == HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU8;
 }
 
 #define HM5065_NUM_FORMATS ARRAY_SIZE(hm5065_formats)
